## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card (a `div` with some content) that rotates 180 deg around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card inner wrapper ---------- */
.card-inner {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transition: transform 0.6s;   /* smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d; /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;  /* hide the back face when turned */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front face styling */
.card-front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

/* Back face styling */
.card-back {
  background: #f8f8f8;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* start rotated */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #555;
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* flip the card on hover */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-inner">
    <div class="card-front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="card-back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `.card` gets `perspective: 1000px;` | Gives depth so the 3D rotation looks natural. |
| **2** | `.card-inner` has `transform-style: preserve-3d;` | Keeps child elements (`.card-front`, `.card-back`) in 3D space. |
| **3** | Both faces have `backface-visibility: hidden;` | Hides the back side when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | On hover, `.card-inner` is rotated 180° around Y‑axis | Creates the flip animation. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more content inside the front/back faces.  
If you want a different axis (X, Z) or a different rotation angle, just change the `rotateY(180deg)` values accordingly.
